christmas some know it as the most  wonderful time of the year a time for  snow hot chocolate family and a sense of  magic in the air others know it as a  time of stress last minute shopping  canceled flights and relatives you'd  rather not be stuck in a room with no  matter how you feel about christmas  there's one thing we can all agree on it  only comes once a year right well that  might be true in most of the world but  the scp foundation came across one  particular little town where the  christmas party never stops for better  or for much much worse scp-784  is a neighborhood in a small texas town  made up of 24 houses and two apartment  buildings every last one of them is  decorated top to bottom in bright  twinkling christmas lights no matter how  hot it is outside and texas summers can  be brutal the ground is always blanketed  with at least 12 centimeters of snow  curiously there is never any visible  snowfall happening in the neighborhood  that would explain this the snow is just  always there it might look inviting from  the outside a quaint little neighborhood  where the snow never melts and the  christmas lights never go out but the  folks at the scp foundation know by now  that things are rarely ever what they  seem all the houses in  scp-784 are occupied by beings referred  to as  scp-784-1 they appear to be completely  ordinary mostly adult humans dressed in  traditional christmas sweaters there are  approximately 300 people living in  scp-784  and they appear to age like normal  people though no deaths of scp-784-1  have ever been observed the citizens of  scp-784 spend their time doing  activities exclusively associated with  christmas and the holiday season they  sing christmas carols perform christmas  pageants throw eggnog festivals give  gifts and decorate their homes when the  sun goes down the activities turn to  acts of christmas-themed vandalism  decorating any object or living thing  deemed not cheerful enough by any means  necessary when a foundation supply  convoy stopped near scp-784 for the  night in order to refuel they got to  experience this maniacal dedication to  the christmas spirit first hand first  the foundation vehicles were egged  drawing the attention of the personnel  on board as the foundation operatives  chased off the egg-based assailants they  left several vehicles unattended when  they returned they found their vehicles  and equipment changed into something a  bit more festive first they noticed that  a humvee had been converted into a  sleigh then upon checking the inventory  of a weapon shipment on board they  realized the fragmentation grenades had  been replaced with glass christmas  ornaments and antlers had been welded  onto the 156 safety helmets in their  possession unsettled by these changes  and the speed at which the seemingly  human instances of  scp-784-1 had been able to make them the  personnel attempted to drive away when  they started their engines they were  shocked at a loud sputtering sound and  bursts of nutmeg-scented smoke while  they were gone their fuel tanks had been  filled with eggnog if this encounter  wasn't enough to demonstrate that  scp-784 was not to be trifled with there  were several incidents of scp foundation  agents entering the bounds of the  neighborhood and failing to adequately  perform the required christmas  celebrations when someone's christmas  cheer is not up to par instances of  scp-784-1 in the vicinity respond  immediately and aggressively  incapacitating the offending person and  forcing them into the nearest house five  different foundation agents have been  abducted in this way so far the first  foundation agent to be abducted was  agent paulson while patrolling through  scp-784 dressed in a rudolph the  red-nosed reindeer sweater and a santa  hat agent paulson made the grave mistake  of wishing a passing person happy  holidays in the blink of an eye the mood  around her darkened eight stone-faced  people with their holly jolly attire  surrounded agent paulson she attempted  to draw her weapon to defend herself but  simply was not fast enough thrashing and  screaming for help agent paulson was  dragged into a nearby home kicking over  an inflatable snowman on the way in next  agent matthews was on night patrol when  a bout of spontaneous caroling broke out  he joined in singing silent night in an  attempt to blend in with the instances  of  scp-784-1 unfortunately he misremembered  the lyrics to the song and began singing  the third verse while everyone else was  on the second while still singing the  citizens overwhelmed agent matthews and  tied him up with a string of decorative  red and green lights agent sanderson who  was supervising the patrol attempted to  intervene and free matthews which  attracted the attention of more  instances of scp-784-1  both agents were overwhelmed by the  crowd restrained and pulled into a home  for what can only be described as  christmas carol reprogramming observers  heard the sound of christmas carols  being sung inside for several days after  while on his patrol agent anderson  tripped and stubbed his toe hard against  a santa claus themed lawn gnome  overwhelmed by pain and irritation  anderson swore loudly and violently for  a duration of 14 seconds at the sound of  his salty language three instances of  scp-784-1  sprang into action and grabbed anderson  before he could react two held his body  in place restraining his arms and  forcing him to his knees the third held  his head still tilting it back and  forcing his mouth open a fourth instance  emerged from a house carrying a cord of  eggnog as anderson struggled to no avail  the eggnog was poured into his mouth  until the court was empty and he  collapsed limply on the ground once he  was rendered unconscious the instances  of  scp-784-1 dragged him inside finally  agent davids was observing the  neighborhood when he was offered a  present by one of the few children in  the town a young girl wearing a sparkly  green and red sweater and a headband  decorated with reindeer antlers davids  accepted the gif with a forced smile and  thanked the little girl but apparently  did not respond with enough enthusiasm  when he failed to give the reaction she  was looking for the little girl tackled  him with a surprising amount of force  grabbing him around his legs and  knocking him to the ground before he  could regain his balance and climb to  his feet several more children emerged  from a nearby house and dragged david's  inside pulling him by his arms and legs  between one and three days after they  were taken the abducted personnel  emerged from the house they were pulled  into they were all dressed in new more  elaborate christmas wear from light up  sweaters to headbands covered in tiny  presents when a supervisor attempted to  extract the foundation personnel the  personnel refused to leave when the  issue was pressed further the instances  of  scp-784-1 around them became  increasingly aggressive and even violent  in their attempt to protect the abducted  agent paulson matthews anderson  sanderson and david's are still within  the boundaries of scp-784  and are all considered lost the official  story is that they died in the line of  duty in order to protect their families  from the truth  scp-784-1's fixation on christmas spirit  doesn't only extend to humans and  inanimate objects any living being  within the walls of scp-784 that doesn't  look festive enough is subject to a  swarm of citizens decorating it and that  includes animals during several patrols  foundation personnel have observed 15  stray cats given red collars with a  small bell seven stray dogs adorned with  reindeer antlers rabbits and raccoons  with santa hats forced onto their heads  and even deer dressed up to resemble the  iconic rudolph out of an abundance of  caution and in an attempt to prevent any  future abductions there have been  extreme limits placed on the number of  staff allowed to patrol inside of  scp-784 the foundation currently only  sends in agents under special  circumstances most notably for a regular  occurrence known as a noel event about  once a month instances of  scp-784-1 will attempt to exit the  boundaries of scp-784  and enter a nearby neighborhood in the  suburban community that's around 784.  each member of the community carries a  15-meter long string of christmas lights  and they wander in a group until they  have found an undecorated house they  will begin to promptly decorate this  house winding the christmas lights  around it until it looks identical to  the rest of the houses in scp-784  it is unclear what happens to the  residents of the chosen house but it is  likely that they are converted into  scp-784-1  much like the abducted foundation agents  naturally the foundation has a vested  interest in preventing scp-784 from  expanding and is dedicated to tracking  and preventing these noel events noel  events do not happen on an exact  schedule but the foundation has become  aware of certain warning signs that one  may be coming prior to a noel event  scp-784-1 becomes more actively festive  during the day notably increasing their  singing decorating and eggnog  consumption when these signs have been  noted a select team of personnel is  ordered to execute procedure 784-c  a preventative measure employed to stop  the noel event from occurring when  procedure 784-c has been ordered to  commence foundation personnel dress up  in santa outfits and position themselves  by the exit points of  scp-784 they sing the classic carol good  king wenslas and pass out non-alcoholic  eggnog to the other personnel stationed  with them naturally this draws the  attention of scp-784-1  unable to resist the allure of holiday  cheer and goodwill towards men once they  have arrived the personnel distribute a  secondary batch of eggnog to scp-784-1  this one mixed with a mild sedative  after the eggnog has been passed out the  foundation personnel are to sing carols  with the citizens of scp-784 as the  sedative takes effect as instances of  scp-784-1 begin to pass out their  neighbors will silently carry them into  their designated homes on their own  until all of them have fallen asleep if  procedure 784-c happens to fail for any  reason the foundation personnel are  instructed to release a sleeping gas  into the town and restrain the citizens  until they have been rendered  unconscious then they are all to be  placed in their homes by personnel if  the members of any nearby communities  express concern a standard cover story  of a neighborhood football watch party  gone a little too far  is released to the public in order to  prevent civilians from accidentally  happening upon  scp-784 the neighborhood has been  disguised as an ordinary gated community  it is surrounded by a 3.5 meter high 0.8  meter thick concrete wall topped with an  electrified steel cable the foundation  is not allowed to prevent non-foundation  personnel from entering in order to  mitigate the risk of a violent reaction  from scp-784-1  however when an individual not related  to the foundation is spotted leaving the  neighborhood they are to be swiftly  detained interrogated and given an  amnesic no foundation personnel are  permitted to enter the neighborhood  unless they are dressed in christmas  attire these personnel must also be  armed with a knowledge of all basic  christmas carols the area is to be  monitored at all times via  foundation-owned weather balloon and the  citizens of scp-784 are to be watched  for unusual behavior and the signs of an  impending noel event scp-784  is currently classified as euclid and is  considered to be largely non-threatening  as long as it continues to be contained  the citizens of scp-784 are not overtly  harming anyone and they don't seem to  want anything more than to celebrate  christmas forever however it's uncertain  how far they would attempt to expand if  noel events were allowed to occur with  no intervention perhaps they would  expand forever forcing eggnog down  throats and strangling houses with  twinkling lights turning the world as we  know it into a twisted snow globe  hopefully we'll never have to find out  just be careful if you're wandering  through the suburbs of texas and hear  the jingling of sleigh bells in july or  you might find yourself on  scp-784's naughty list now go check out  trapped in a game scp-1733  season opener and the skin stealers  scp-3333  tower for more places you hope to never  find yourself
 

